1
00:00:08,425 --> 00:00:10,010
The cast can't
hang out off-camera.

2
00:00:10,677 --> 00:00:12,137
It'll kill the chemistry.

3
00:00:30,947 --> 00:00:32,365
How'd they even meet?

4
00:00:35,493 --> 00:00:37,662
Their meetings
are all staggered.

5
00:00:38,246 --> 00:00:40,540
They were bound to
cross paths eventually.

6
00:00:43,835 --> 00:00:46,463
Nobody gets this cozy
the first time they meet.

7
00:00:47,881 --> 00:00:50,675
Then it won't feel like
they're meeting for the first time.

8
00:00:54,679 --> 00:00:57,182
We need a stronger opening
for episode one.

9
00:01:09,569 --> 00:01:10,779
What are you thinking?

10
00:01:12,238 --> 00:01:13,615
What you said
about the opening.

11
00:01:17,911 --> 00:01:19,162
Well, it's
already happened.

12
00:01:19,871 --> 00:01:21,456
Let's make it work.

13
00:01:21,456 --> 00:01:22,665
No.

14
00:01:26,961 --> 00:01:29,714
If it's wrong, we stop.

15
00:01:37,722 --> 00:01:40,183
What I mean is...

16
00:01:40,934 --> 00:01:42,936
How do we make it work?

17
00:01:45,438 --> 00:01:46,564
Rewrite the script.

18
00:01:46,564 --> 00:01:48,566
Don't call Episode One
"First Meeting."

19
00:01:48,566 --> 00:01:50,193
"Reunited."

20
00:01:52,083 --> 00:01:54,291
Reunited...

21
00:02:44,291 --> 00:02:53,625
[Host: Is this
your first time meeting?]

22
00:03:18,031 --> 00:03:19,073
Thanks.

23
00:03:23,208 --> 00:03:26,000
It all started
with a locker key.

24
00:03:28,166 --> 00:03:31,125
That's when I learned
his name was

25
00:03:31,916 --> 00:03:33,041
Cole.

26
00:03:47,393 --> 00:03:48,436
You're blocking my way.

27
00:03:58,529 --> 00:03:59,572
Crap.

28
00:04:02,200 --> 00:04:02,617
Hey.

29
00:04:02,617 --> 00:04:03,743
Sorry, I was wondering...

30
00:04:03,743 --> 00:04:04,953
Can I borrow
your add maths homework?

31
00:04:08,665 --> 00:04:10,541
Add maths.

32
00:04:10,541 --> 00:04:11,501
Can I copy it?

33
00:04:14,003 --> 00:04:14,750
Yeah...

34
00:04:14,750 --> 00:04:16,291
For the first two months

35
00:04:16,291 --> 00:04:17,125
as seatmates,

36
00:04:17,125 --> 00:04:18,916
we barely talked.

37
00:04:19,458 --> 00:04:22,291
Back then, I'd go to school
just to sleep

38
00:04:22,541 --> 00:04:23,375
and copy homework.

39
00:04:24,500 --> 00:04:25,333
Can I copy
your physics?

40
00:04:26,083 --> 00:04:28,458
And of course, band.

41
00:04:31,813 --> 00:04:33,356
You play guitar?

42
00:04:34,440 --> 00:04:36,734
Wanna start
a band with me?

43
00:04:36,734 --> 00:04:38,111
I need a guitarist.

44
00:04:39,070 --> 00:04:40,738
No.

45
00:04:43,825 --> 00:04:44,826
Please.

46
00:04:45,535 --> 00:04:47,287
How many people
are in it?

47
00:04:47,287 --> 00:04:49,205
Just me.
With you, we'd have two.

48
00:04:50,581 --> 00:04:52,083
We'll find the rest later.

49
00:04:52,083 --> 00:04:53,167
Then when we recruit,

50
00:04:53,167 --> 00:04:55,587
we can say
we've already got two.

51
00:04:56,916 --> 00:04:57,583
And that's how

52
00:04:58,833 --> 00:05:01,666
two complete opposites

53
00:05:02,875 --> 00:05:04,083
who started out copying homework

54
00:05:04,958 --> 00:05:06,333
ended up starting a band

55
00:05:07,083 --> 00:05:08,208
and slowly became

56
00:05:08,625 --> 00:05:10,958
best friends.

57
00:05:12,958 --> 00:05:13,583
What?

58
00:05:14,291 --> 00:05:14,916
It's messed up.

59
00:05:23,906 --> 00:05:24,907
Chen Yaowei,

60
00:05:25,867 --> 00:05:27,702
you lose your key
every time.

61
00:05:28,625 --> 00:05:29,708
This is the spare.

62
00:05:29,704 --> 00:05:30,872
I'll hang on to it.

63
00:05:30,872 --> 00:05:32,206
Why should you?

64
00:05:32,206 --> 00:05:34,292
In case you ever
lock yourself out

65
00:05:34,292 --> 00:05:35,626
or lose your key,

66
00:05:35,626 --> 00:05:37,879
I'll still have the spare.

67
00:05:48,583 --> 00:05:49,666
Maybe

68
00:05:51,791 --> 00:05:54,333
we'd become something
more than friends.

69
00:06:49,283 --> 00:06:51,536
Hey...

70
00:06:51,536 --> 00:06:52,995
Have you been
waiting long?

71
00:07:13,975 --> 00:07:14,809
Can we

72
00:07:16,144 --> 00:07:17,728
stop waiting?
